{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"JLSEC-2026-934","published":"2026-07-30T16:02:27.435Z","modified":"2026-07-30T18:35:51.508638609Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-22770","EUVD-2026-3401","GHSA-39h3-g67r-7g3c"],"summary":"ImageMagick releases an invalid pointer in BilateralBlur when memory allocation fails","details":"ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. The BilateralBlurImage method will allocate a set of double buffers inside AcquireBilateralTLS. But, in versions prior to 7.1.2-13, the last element in the set is not properly initialized. This will result in a release of an invalid pointer inside DestroyBilateralTLS when the memory allocation fails. Version 7.1.2-13 contains a patch for the issue.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/ImageMagick_jll?uuid=c73af94c-d91f-53ed-93a7-00f77d67a9d7"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.2023+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-934.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/3e0330721020e0c5bb52e4b77c347527dd71658e"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-39h3-g67r-7g3c"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-39h3-g67r-7g3c"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/dlemstra/Magick.NET/releases/tag/14.10.2"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-22770"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-22770","id":"CVE-2026-22770","imported":"2026-07-30T14:08:44.587Z","modified":"2026-06-17T10:20:23.690Z","published":"2026-01-20T01:15:57.153Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-22770"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3